# AIMS feature inventory

This document is the product-content source for the AIMS features page. Final availability depends on the modules, integrations, and custom work agreed for an institution.

## AIMS academic and administrative modules

### Admission management

- Move an enquiry or application through review and approval stages.
- Maintain applicant and student data cards.
- Allocate transfer certificates through the defined workflow.

### Course allocation

- Capture student preferences.
- Apply seat availability and reservation rules.
- Run automated allotment based on the configured criteria.

### Internal marks

- Bring Moodle activity marks into the academic record.
- Apply custom mark weightage.
- Add marks from offline activities.

### OBE and academic reporting

- Map course outcomes, programme outcomes, and programme-specific outcomes.
- Calculate attainment.
- Prepare OBE and NAAC-related reporting workflows.

### Timetables, attendance, and reporting

- Manage student batches, academic years, and FYUGP course allocation.
- Create department and class schedules.
- Generate attendance sessions and record attendance on mobile devices.
- Prepare AISHE and institutional activity reports.

### Communication and integrations

- Send WhatsApp notifications, including assignment and quiz reminders.
- Integrate supported biometric attendance devices, including eSSL devices.
- Discuss approved third-party integrations where they support an academic workflow.

### Optional institutional modules

- Parent or guardian access to selected attendance and grade information.
- Library-management workflows.
- Institution promotional-content uploads.

## Moodle learning capabilities

- Online courses, notes, learning resources, and tutorial sharing.
- Assignments, assessments, and quizzes, including timed attempts and supported question types.
- H5P interactive learning activities and interactive video lessons.
- Live classes through BigBlueButton, Google Meet, or Zoom when included in the setup.
- Course engagement, activity completion, and progress tracking.
- Mobile access. Moodle’s official app can support offline course-content access when the Moodle site enables it.
- Role-based access for administrators, teachers, and students.
- Manual or self-registration where the institution’s enrolment process allows it.

## Module and workflow approach

- Select the modules your institution needs rather than adopting every module.
- Configure approved workflows around current academic and administrative processes.
- Reuse course materials across batches and academic years through Moodle courses.
- Discuss custom modules, design changes, content-development support, and integrations as part of the project scope.
